infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Head-based vs tail-based sampling
  desc Same final stored volume — opposite cost and accuracy profiles
  compares
    - label Head-based
      children
        - label Decides at trace start
          desc SDK drops before any span is emitted
        - label Keeps 1–10% of traces
          desc Uniform random, predictable low cost
        - label Zero collector cost on drops
          desc No spans, no network bytes for dropped traces
        - label Misses rare errors and slow tails
          desc Uniform sample under-represents the events you most need
    - label Tail-based
      children
        - label Decides after the tree finishes
          desc Buffers every span 30–60 s, then applies policy
        - label Keeps 100% of errors and slow traces
          desc Drops fast successes at a 0.5–5% base rate
        - label Collector scales with raw traffic
          desc Every span flows through the collector even if dropped
        - label Most accurate, highest overhead
          desc CPU and memory track total request volume, not kept volume
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
